1. d4 d5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. Bf4 c5 4. e3 e6 5. Nb5 { Nb5 is often a good plan against c5. } { [%cal Gb5c7,Gf4c7,Gc7e8,Gc7a8] } 5... Na6 { Black's knight is tied up defending our fork threat . The rook tied up to the a pawn as a defense. We disabled two of black's pieces with our knight. } { [%cal Ra6c7,Ra8a7,Gb5a7,Gb5c7] } 6. c3 Be7 7. Bd3 O-O 8. a4 b6 9. Nf3 Bb7 10. Ne5 Nd7 11. Qh5 { [%cal Gh5h7,Gd3h7] } 11... f5 12. g4 *


