1. d4 Nf6 2. Nc3 d5 3. Bf4 Bf5 4. f3 (4. e3 e6 5. Nf3 { e.g. } 5... a6 (5... c5?! 6. Bxb8!? (6. Nb5 Na6 7. c3 $14 { is good again }) 6... Qxb8 7. Bb5+ Kd8 8. Ne5 Qc7) 6. Ne5 { planning g4 and h4 again }) 4... e6 5. g4 Bg6 6. h4 h6 (6... h5 7. g5 Nfd7 8. e3 (8. e4) 8... Bd6 (8... c5?! 9. Nb5 Na6 10. c3 Be7 11. Bd3 { with an edge for White }) 9. Nh3 Nc6 10. Nb5 Bxf4 11. Nxf4 Bf5 12. Bd3 Ne7 { White for preference }) 7. e3 c5 (7... a6 { is an alternative e.g. } 8. Bd3 Bxd3 9. cxd3!? c5 10. dxc5 Bxc5 11. d4 Bd6 12. Nge2 { White can put his king on f2 and await developments }) 8. h5 Bh7 9. Nb5 Na6 10. c3 Be7 11. Bd3 Bxd3 12. Qxd3 Nd7 13. Ne2 O-O 14. a4 Bf6 15. Bd6 Re8 16. f4 Nb6 17. g5 hxg5 18. h6 g6 19. fxg5 Bxg5 20. h7+ Kg7 21. Be5+ f6 22. Nd6 Rh8 23. Nf4 Bxf4 24. Bxf4 g5 25. O-O-O Nc4 26. Rh6 Kxh6 27. Nf7+ Kg7 28. Nxd8 Raxd8 { 1 d4 Nf6 2 Nc3 d5 3 Bf4 Bf5 - ?, A complete repertoire on the London
System with Nc3: Chapter 3, https://lichess.org/study/Kp6cbyEp/WkCEIATy, } *


