1. d4 Nf6 2. Bf4 d5 3. Nc3 a6 { Stops Nb5. } { [%cal Ra6b5,Bc3b5] } 4. e3 e6 5. g4!? { Interesting idea - kick black knight and grab some space on king side with g & h pawns. } { [%cal Bg4g5,Yg5f6] } 5... c5 6. g5 Nfd7 7. Nf3 { Simply develops. } 7... Nc6 8. a3 b5 { Black in principle counterattacks on the opposite side. } 9. h4 Bb7 { Good square for the bishop, also it can helps to castle queen side since white pushed g & h pawns already. } { [%cal Yb7g2] } 10. h5 Nb6 11. Ne5 Nxe5 12. Bxe5 Nc4 13. Bxc4 { Damages the pawn structure and eliminates knight that took long path to the c4 square. } { [%cal Bb8d7,Bd7b6,Bb6c4] } 13... dxc4 14. Rg1 f6 15. Bf4 Qd7 16. h6 O-O-O 17. Qe2 cxd4 18. exd4 Qxd4 19. Rd1 Qxf4 20. Qxe6+ Kc7 21. Qf7+ Be7?? 22. Qxe7+ Kc8 23. hxg7 Rxd1+ 24. Nxd1 Rg8 25. Qf8+ Kc7 26. Qxg8 { 1-0, Carlsen, M. (2832) - Caruana, F. (2808), Import,
https://lichess.org/toKk31dU, 2017.11.05 } *


