1. d4 Nf6 2. Nc3 d5 3. Bf4 Bf5 4. f3 { With plan of pushing black light-squared bishop around and grabbing some space on king side. } { [%cal Bg2g4,Bh2h4] } 4... e6 5. g4 Bg6 6. h4 { [%cal Bh4h5,Rh5g6] } 6... h6 (6... h5 { Alternative. } 7. g5 { [%cal Rg5f6] }) 7. e3 c5 8. h5 Bh7 9. Nb5 { Standard plan. } { [%csl Yc7][%cal Yb5c7,Yf4c7,Rc7e8,Rc7a8] } 9... Na6 { Knight on a6 is stupid, has to guard c7 square. } { [%csl Ya6][%cal Ga6c7] } 10. c3 Be7 { It makes sense to exchange light-squared bishop and develop queen to d3. } { [%cal Bf1d3,Rd1d3] } 11. Bd3 Bxd3 12. Qxd3 Nd7 13. Ne2 O-O 14. a4 { Cements knight on b5. It cannot be easy kicked from the outpost and controls good squares. } { [%csl Rc7,Rd6][%cal Ga4b5,Ya7a6,Rb5d6,Rb5c7] } 14... Bf6 { Losing control over d6 square. } { [%csl Yd6][%cal Bf4d6] } 15. Bd6 Re8 16. f4 { White starts attack on king side. } { [%cal Bf4f5,Bg4g5,Bh5h6] } 16... Nb6 17. g5 $140 { With an idea of shred open black king. } { [%cal Be1c1,Ba1g1,Yg1g8,Yh1h8] } 17... hxg5 18. h6 g6 19. fxg5 { [%csl Bg5,Bh6] } 19... Bxg5 20. h7+ Kg7 21. Be5+ f6 22. Nd6 Rh8 (22... fxe5 23. dxe5 { Powerful knight, controlling a lot of squares in black camp. } { [%csl Rd6][%cal Yd6f7,Yd6e8,Yd6c8,Yd6f5] }) 23. Nf4 Bxf4 24. Bxf4 g5 { Stoping Bh6. } 25. O-O-O { White simple continues with plan of bringing heavy pieces to the attack. } { [%cal Bd1g1] } 25... Nc4 (25... gxf4 26. Qg6+ Kxg6 27. Rdg1#) 26. Rh6 Kxh6 (26... Kf8 27. Rxf6+ Kg7 (27... Ke7 28. Rf7#) 28. Qg6#) 27. Nf7+ Kg7 28. Nxd8 Raxd8 29. b3 Nb6 30. Rg1 Rxh7 31. e4 Kh8 32. e5 gxf4 33. Qg6 Rf8 34. exf6 { 1-0, Baadur Aleksandrovich Jobava 2688 - Shakhriyar Mamedyarov 2799,
World Rapid Championship, Dubai UAE (3.1), 2014.06.16 } *


