1. d4 d5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. Bf4 c5 4. e3 a6 (4... Nc6?? { literally played in 36 of my 92 games }) (4... cxd4 5. exd4 a6 6. Nf3 Nc6 7. Ne5 { i seem to only remember this a third of the time } (7. Be2 Bg4 8. O-O e6 9. Ne5 Bxe2 10. Nxe2 Bd6 11. c4 dxc4 12. Nxc6 bxc6 13. Qa4 Bxf4 14. Nxf4 Qxd4? { K_A_L_E - NM GMcanty, 0-1, -, https://lichess.org/VdLttwJh } (14... O-O!)) 7... Qb6 8. Nxc6 Qxc6 9. Bd3 Bg4 10. Qd2 { K_A_L_E - Sadegh_mahmoody1971, 1/2-1/2, -, https://lichess.org/cFFB4duU } (10. f3 { [%cal Gg2g4] })) (4... e6 5. Nf3 (5. Nb5 Na6 6. a4 Be7 7. Be2 { K_A_L_E - darlenhalo, 1-0, -, https://lichess.org/zLu6rjCP }) 5... Bd6! { this is a nice point, i could have avoided this if i remembered the Nb5 point K_A_L_E - Selensky_Andrey, 0-1, -, https://lichess.org/bELhCgCU }) 5. dxc5 Nc6 { far and away most common response } (5... e6 6. Na4 Bxc5 (6... Qa5+ 7. c3 Bd7?? 8. Nb6 { K_A_L_E - laikom, 1-0, -, https://lichess.org/2qaXhfBP }) 7. Nxc5 Qa5+ 8. c3 Qxc5 9. Nf3 Nc6 10. Qd2? { [%cal Gf6e4] } (10. Bd3 { crucial }) 10... Ne4 { K_A_L_E - ghazzarian, 0-1, -, https://lichess.org/3gQGOVAI }) 6. Nf3 Bg4 7. Be2 e6 8. Na4 Bxc5? (8... Nh5 9. c3 $16 { K_A_L_E - FM chesszerorfl, 0-1, -, https://lichess.org/IHXmG78A }) 9. Nxc5 Qa5+ 10. c3? (10. Nd2! Bxe2 11. Nxb7! { very cool idea }) *


[Event "The Jobava London System (Rapport-Jobava System) - Complete Repertoire: Example Games #1 - Hikaru Nakamura 2767 - Anish Giri 2776"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
