1. d4 { This was a game played by Magnus Carlsen with the white pieces against Jeffery Xiong with the black pieces, played on Lichess.org. Jeffery Xiong made a mistake in the opening in which Magnus Carlsen pressed and took the initiative. Black went on to resign the game. } 1... Nf6 2. Nc3 d5 3. Bf4 { D01 Rapport-Jobava System } 3... e6 4. e3 Bb4 5. Ne2 O-O 6. a3 Be7 7. Ng1?! { Perhaps unnecessary, but Magnus is Magnus, I think he was playing drunk in here This is how you play Chess after two bottles of wine. } 7... c5 8. Nf3 Nh5 9. dxc5 Nxf4 10. exf4 Bxc5 11. Bd3 { Uncanny, weakens the kingside. Prone to attack. } 11... g6?! { (-0.71 → -0.03) Inaccuracy. Qf6 was best. } (11... Qf6) 12. h4 Nc6 13. h5 { Magnus went on and shoved the h pawn over the board. } 13... Qf6 14. Qd2 { White's assault continues up to this day! } 14... e5?? { (0.70 → 5.34) Blunder. Rb8 was best. } (14... Rb8 15. Kf1 b5 16. g3 b4 17. axb4 Rxb4 18. Kg2 Bd6 19. Qe3 Rxb2 20. Nb5 Bb8 21. hxg6) 15. Nxd5 Qd6 16. Bc4 b5 17. Ba2 exf4 18. O-O-O b4 19. hxg6 hxg6 20. Ng5 Bf5 { g4 is perhaps stronger since this eventually adds up the pressure on the kingside. But who knows white is already winning in here. Black is forced to give up the rook. } 21. Nh7? { (7.50 → 4.09) Mistake. g4 was best. } (21. g4) 21... Rfd8? { Black is forced to give up the rook but nyeah? (4.09 → 7.46) Mistake. Bd4 was best. } (21... Bd4 22. g4) 22. Nhf6+ Kf8 23. Rh8+ Kg7 24. Rh7+ Kf8 25. Rdh1 { 1-0, Magnus Carlsen 2863 - Jeffery Xiong 2709, The Rapport Jobava System: Complete Repertoire: ____Example Game #2 Magnus Carlsen - Jeffery Xiong____, Lichess.org, } *


