1. d4 d5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. Bf4 { D01 Rapport-Jobava System } 3... e6 { For example } 4. e3 (4. Nb5 Na6 (4... Bd6) 5. a3 { Prevents Bb4 } (5. e3 c6 (5... Bb4+) 6. Nc3 Bb4 7. Bxa6 bxa6 8. Nf3 O-O) 5... c6 6. Nc3 Be7 7. e3 O-O 8. Bd3 (8. Qf3) (8. g4) (8. f3) (8. h4 b5 9. Nf3 Bb7 10. Ne5) (8. Qd2 b5 9. Bd3 b4 10. axb4 Nxb4 11. O-O-O) 8... c5) (4. a3 { Also possible for Bb4 prevention. }) 4... c5 (4... a6 { Preventing Nb5, is often played by people who know what they're doing. } { [%cal Gc3b5] } 5. g4! { The queen is already protecting this square so we can push g4. } 5... c5 6. g5 Nfd7 7. h4 Nc6 8. Nf3 { Casabianka - Precise_Chess, 1-0, -, https://lichess.org/QXLVYoEW See the game attached to understand this line better. }) (4... Bb4 { Is an annoying move for Black. }) 5. Nb5 { Is a common line: } 5... Na6 6. c3 Be7 7. a4 { This knight is excellent on b5! Jobava, Ba - Yudin, S., 1/2-1/2, FIDE World Rapid 2014, https://lichess.org/8fxMtqrW } { [%csl Bb5][%cal Ga4b5] } 7... O-O 8. h3 Ne8 9. Nf3 Nac7 10. Nxc7 Nxc7 11. Bd3 Ne8 12. a5?! { (1.03 → 0.42) Inaccuracy. dxc5 was best. } (12. dxc5 Bxc5 13. O-O Nf6 14. Qc2 Bd6 15. Rfd1 h6 16. a5 Bxf4 17. exf4 Qc7 18. Qa4 Bd7) 12... Nf6 13. O-O Bd7 14. Ne5 a6 15. Qb1?! { (0.99 → 0.22) Inaccuracy. b3 was best. } (15. b3) 15... Bb5 16. dxc5 Bxc5 17. Bxb5 axb5 18. Bg5?! { (0.17 → -0.71) Inaccuracy. Qd3 was best. } (18. Qd3) 18... Be7 19. Qd3 Rxa5 20. Rxa5 Qxa5 21. b4?! { (-0.92 → -1.62) Inaccuracy. Bxf6 was best. } (21. Bxf6 gxf6 22. Nf3 b4 23. Qd4 h6 24. Qg4+ Kh7 25. cxb4 Qxb4 26. Qxb4 Bxb4 27. Ra1 Kg6) 21... Qc7 22. Nf3 Qc4 23. Qxc4 bxc4 24. Ra1 h6 25. Bxf6 Bxf6 26. Nd4 Rb8 27. Kf1 Kf8 28. Ke2 Ke7 29. Kd2 Bxd4 30. exd4 Kd6 31. h4 f6?! { (-1.72 → -1.13) Inaccuracy. g5 was best. } (31... g5) 32. f4?! { (-1.13 → -1.85) Inaccuracy. h5 was best. } (32. h5 e5) 32... h5 33. Ra7 Kc6 34. Ra5?! { (-1.67 → -2.68) Inaccuracy. Ke3 was best. } (34. Ke3 Rd8) 34... Re8?! { (-2.68 → -1.58) Inaccuracy. g5 was best. } (34... g5) 35. Rc5+ Kd6 36. Rb5 Re7 37. g3 g6 38. Ke3 Kc7 39. Ra5 Re8 40. Rc5+ Kb6 41. Ra5 Rb8 42. Ra1 Kc6 43. Ra5 Kd6 44. Ra1 e5 45. fxe5+ fxe5 46. dxe5+ Kxe5 47. Ra5 Rf8?! { (-1.82 → -0.68) Inaccuracy. b6 was best. } (47... b6) 48. Rb5 Rf1 49. Rxb7 Rd1 50. Ke2 Rg1 51. Re7+ Kd6 52. Re3 Rb1 53. Kf3?! { (0.00 → -0.92) Inaccuracy. Kd2 was best. } (53. Kd2 Rb2+ 54. Kc1 Rg2 55. Rf3 Rg1+ 56. Kc2 Kc7 57. Kd2 Rg2+ 58. Kc1 Kd6 59. Re3 Rf2) 53... Rf1+?! { (-0.92 → 0.00) Inaccuracy. Rb2 was best. } (53... Rb2 54. g4) 54. Ke2 { ½-½, Jobava, Ba 2713 - Yudin, S. 2546, FIDE World Rapid 2014, Dubai UAE (7.14), 2014.06.17 } *


